project lead and indeed,

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:20.930
so this always fits like the position

00:11:20.930 --> 00:11:23.010
where just like from all directions

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:24.900
you're being put under pressure.

00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:27.290
Now back at all the people in
the Firm Learning community,

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:29.770
I know several of you
are also still graduates

00:11:29.770 --> 00:11:31.260
or maybe in the first years

00:11:31.260 --> 00:11:34.300
thinking about potentially
joining consulting.

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:36.250
And I trust you would
all be very interested

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:39.210
to get your insights into
the interview process,

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:42.630
your silver bullet of how to be successful

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:43.780
in consulting interviews.

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:46.120
So, what tips do you have to share here?

00:11:47.030 --> 00:11:48.910
- So I think in the moment
where you conduct the interview

00:11:50.284 --> 00:11:52.930
with the team, I think you
have to be very structured

00:11:52.930 --> 00:11:55.900
in regards to how you give your answers

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:59.040
that everyone can really
relate to what you're saying.

00:11:59.040 --> 00:12:01.120
And you should have
prepared good questions,

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:03.310
which are really meaningful questions.

00:12:03.310 --> 00:12:05.270
And that sends what you wanna know

00:12:05.270 --> 00:12:07.540
as a potential future consultant,

00:12:07.540 --> 00:12:08.940
but also what could be interesting

00:12:08.940 --> 00:12:11.270
in regards to the whole conversation.

00:12:11.270 --> 00:12:14.120
And then it's also super
important that you stay authentic

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:15.250
in the way you are.

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:17.870
So if you're not a very
strong communicator,

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:19.940
just don't try to overdo it or anything,

00:12:19.940 --> 00:12:22.680
just to stay true to
yourself and just be natural

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:24.930
in the way that you talk, communicate

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:27.060
and act in the interview, I think

00:12:27.060 --> 00:12:29.240
that's very important.
- Makes sense, yeah.

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:31.950
- In terms of preparation,
maybe I give you an overview

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:34.660
of how our interviews are structured.

00:12:34.660 --> 00:12:38.510
So they usually take
either a whole a morning

00:12:38.510 --> 00:12:39.950
or a whole afternoon.

00:12:39.950 --> 00:12:43.180
It starts with an analytical test

00:12:43.180 --> 00:12:45.070
that takes approximately an hour.

00:12:45.070 --> 00:12:48.730
And then you will have
three interviews in a row.

00:12:48.730 --> 00:12:51.780
You will have an interview
with a project manager

00:12:51.780 --> 00:12:53.520
or a senior project manager,

00:12:53.520 --> 00:12:57.260
then one with the principal
and one with an MD.

00:12:57.260 --> 00:13:01.700
And you will do one is HR interview

00:13:01.700 --> 00:13:03.870
where you are asked questions.

00:13:03.870 --> 00:13:05.920
One is a case interview.

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:07.920
And the last one with the MD is the one

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:11.200
where you usually also
present part of your work.

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:13.820
So you have time to prepare a presentation

00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:16.890
already beforehand, and you
present this presentation

00:13:16.890 --> 00:13:17.943
then to the MD.

00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:20.240
In terms of preparation,

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:22.860
my suggestion would be
for the analytical tests

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:26.480
to practice your calculation skills.

00:13:26.480 --> 00:13:31.010
So this is something I had
to experience myself too.

00:13:31.010 --> 00:13:34.120
So you think, yeah,
multiplying, dividing, easy,

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:36.830
I can do it.

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:39.030
It's better to practice it beforehand

00:13:39.030 --> 00:13:42.480
because it's not so
easy to remember things

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:44.230
you learned 20 years ago.

00:13:44.230 --> 00:13:47.873
So that would be one
suggestion from my side.

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:53.400
In terms of the case, so we
are procurement consulting.

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:57.480
So I would suggest have a
look at procurement levers.

00:13:57.480 --> 00:14:01.610
So what are typically
levers that we apply,

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:03.340
because it's very likely

00:14:03.340 --> 00:14:05.968
that you will get a procurement case.

